From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc/mm: do not grow max_pfn for ZONE_DEVICE ranges

add_pages() unconditionally calls update_end_of_memory_vars(), so a
devm_memremap_pages() of a MEMORY_DEVICE_PRIVATE range (which lives in a
fake physical window near the top of the physical address space) raises
max_pfn far beyond the end of RAM.

dma_direct_get_required_mask() derives a device's DMA requirement from
max_pfn, and dma_go_direct() re-evaluates it on every mapping for a
dma_ops_bypass device. On powernv, a PCI device whose DMA mask is smaller
than the bypass window (e.g. amdgpu, 44 bits) is given the TVE#0 "64-bit
DMA iommu bypass" by pnv_pci_ioda_dma_64bit_bypass(): a static 256MB-TCE
table mapping dma = phys + 4GB, while the PE's software iommu_table is
left in place. Once max_pfn exceeds the device mask, dma_go_direct()
starts returning false and every subsequent mapping goes through
dma_iommu_ops: IOVAs are allocated from, and TCEs written into, the
software table the hardware is no longer consulting. The static table
translates those IOVAs linearly onto unrelated RAM. Nothing faults.

Observed on an IBM 8335-GCA (POWER8, hash MMU, 64K pages) with two
Radeon Pro V620 (Navi21): amdgpu registers 30GB of VRAM as device-private
memory for KFD SVM, after which all user-VM GPU access to system memory
returns garbage while kernel buffers mapped before the registration keep
working. With 4K pages the registration fails (linear map range) so the
bug is masked. Skipping the max_pfn update for ZONE_DEVICE ranges (which
are not RAM and can never be DMA targets) restores correct DMA with HMM
fully enabled.

The powernv pseudo-bypass leaving a stale iommu_table attached is a
second problem: any later growth of max_pfn (memory hotplug) would
re-trigger the same silent corruption. That deserves its own fix in
pci-ioda.c.

Signed-off-by: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/mm/mem.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/powerpc/mm/mem.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/mm/mem.c
@@ -135,9 +135,17 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

-	/* update max_pfn, max_low_pfn and high_memory */
-	update_end_of_memory_vars(start_pfn << PAGE_SHIFT,
-				  nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT);
+	/*
+	 * Do not let ZONE_DEVICE (e.g. MEMORY_DEVICE_PRIVATE) ranges grow
+	 * max_pfn: they are not RAM and can never be DMA targets, but
+	 * dma_direct_get_required_mask() derives the device DMA requirement
+	 * from max_pfn, and on powernv a dma_ops_bypass device whose PE uses
+	 * the TVE#0 64-bit pseudo-bypass table would silently fall back to
+	 * the (now stale) iommu_table path once max_pfn exceeds its mask.
+	 */
+	if (!params->pgmap)
+		update_end_of_memory_vars(start_pfn << PAGE_SHIFT,
+					  nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT);

 	return ret;
 }
